# Extra CA certificates for upstream data services (NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# kart.miljodirektoratet.no serves an INCOMPLETE TLS CHAIN: it sends its leaf
# certificate twice and never sends the GlobalSign AlphaSSL intermediate that
# signed it. Browsers paper over this by fetching the missing intermediate from
# the certificate's AIA extension; Node and curl do not, so every request from
# the backend failed with UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE. That killed the
# shipped `wildlife-areas` overlay outright in production (cold tiles 502'd
# while cached ones kept drawing, so nothing looked wrong) and blocks the
# Naturbase / anadromous-water inputs the Fish & Hunt engine needs.
#
# Supplying the intermediate does NOT widen trust: it chains to GlobalSign Root
# CA - R6, which is already in Node's root store. All this does is complete a
# chain the server should have completed itself.
#
# WHEN IT GOES STALE
# The intermediate below expires 2027-05-21, and the server's leaf expires
# 2027-01-03 — a renewal may well come with a different intermediate, at which
# point requests to that host start failing again. That is precisely why the N7
# upstream probes ship alongside this: `miljodirektoratet-tls` on the status
# page is the thing that will tell us, instead of another silent dead layer.
# To refresh: read the CA Issuers URI out of the live certificate and replace
# the block below with it.
#
#   openssl s_client -connect kart.miljodirektoratet.no:443 \
#     -servername kart.miljodirektoratet.no </dev/null 2>/dev/null \
#     | openssl x509 -noout -text | grep -A2 'Authority Information Access'
#   curl -sS <that URI> | openssl x509 -inform DER
#
# subject=C = BE, O = GlobalSign nv-sa, CN = GlobalSign GCC R6 AlphaSSL CA 2025
# issuer=OU = GlobalSign Root CA - R6, O = GlobalSign, CN = GlobalSign
# notBefore=May 21 02:36:52 2025 GMT
# notAfter=May 21 00:00:00 2027 GMT
#
